 "source": "/en/admin/SecurityPageAccess.jsp - Page Access tab. Read by GET with ?UserClass={id}; no click, no save.",
 "methodNote": "The UserClass selector IS a GET parameter - `?UserClass=7889` re-renders the whole matrix server-side, and the returned page's <select> confirms which class is selected. I verified the matrix actually changes between classes before trusting any value. IMPORTANT correction to my own earlier caution: the bare page is NOT an 'unselected default' - it loads with `Default Security` (7884) genuinely selected, and that class really does deny almost everything. My earlier note that the all-NoAccess snapshot was 'not evidence' was right to withhold judgement but wrong about the cause.",
 "userClassCount": 10,
 "headline": {
  "question": "Q-BBW-12 gate 3 - is per-user-class Page Access what suppresses the `Equipment Contract` root at AF?",
  "answer": "NO. REFUTED.",
  "evidence": "`Equipment Contract` page access is GRANTED at AF for 8 of 10 user classes - `Delete` for Full Access, Lease Admin, Lease Admin Accounting, Lease Admin Manager and System Administrator; `View` for Lease Admin Client, Lease Admin Client - Allowances and Lease Admin View. It is denied only by `Default Security` (which denies essentially everything, including Contract) and `Lease Admin Mail`. In every class that grants Contract at all, Equipment Contract is granted at the SAME level - the two are indistinguishable in this matrix.",
  "consequence": "All three hypothesised gates are OPEN at American Freight, yet the root does not render: gate 1 `Allow Equipment Contracts?` = Yes; gate 2 the menu structure (id 41087, 5 groups, 64 nodes) is present in Manage Top Menu; gate 3 page access is granted for 8 of 10 classes. **The three-gate model does not close by elimination.** Whatever suppresses the root is a fourth mechanism, not yet identified.",
  "alsoRuledOut": "No single user class can explain the observed 4-root navigation. Every class that grants Contract also grants Equipment Contract. `Lease Admin Mail` is the only class granting Contract while denying Equipment Contract - but it also denies Location and Facility, which DO render. So the rendered root set is not the page-access grant set for any class, alone or as a union."
 },
 "secondFinding": {
  "observation": "`Program` is granted (`Default`) by all 10 classes and `Delete` by System Administrator, yet `Program` does NOT render as a navigation root at AF.",
  "why it matters": "This is an independent counterexample to 'page access determines which roots render', found in the same data. Page access being open is demonstrably not sufficient for a root to appear. Note also that AF's root LABELLED `Portfolio` carries requestedProjectEntityType=`Program`, while the separate `Program` menu structure (id 3851) is the one that stays hidden - so the two must not be conflated."
 },
